# Read from the build context root, which is now the repository root rather than
# backend/. Every pattern below is anchored there — this is why the paths carry a
# `backend/` prefix and why several use `**/`: a bare `.env` would no longer match
# `backend/.env`, and that file holds a live OPENAI_API_KEY.
**/node_modules
**/.env
.git
**/coverage
**/data/private
**/*.log

# Patterns match the whole relative path, so a bare `.DS_Store` would only catch
# the one at the root. macOS scatters them through every transcript folder.
**/.DS_Store

# The image serves; it never ingests. At runtime the only thing needed from
# transcripts/ is the spine named by CURRICULUM_PATH, so the 87 lessons and the
# concept-graph cache stay out of the build context — about 4.8 MB of 5.4 MB.
# Keep backend/transcripts/class-subtitle/curriculum.json.
**/transcripts/**/*.vtt
**/transcripts/**/*.srt
**/transcripts/**/concept-graph*.json
**/transcripts/**/transcript-manifest.json

# Documentation and tests are not needed to run the server. frontend/public is
# deliberately absent from this list: the server serves it.
**/*.md
backend/test
